Here is the complete, end-to-end database script to build and populate your Dynamic Workflow Engine. This covers the table creations, the required alteration to your existing table, and the exact data inserts for both Workflow_3 (the 3-level flow) and Workflow_4 (the 4-level flow).
Execute these commands in your Oracle database.
### 1. Schema Creation & Table Alteration
First, we create the two dynamic tables and update your existing VOUCHER_POSTING table to store numeric Role IDs instead of strings.
```sql
-- Create the Routing Table (Determines which workflow a Maker triggers)
CREATE TABLE WORKFLOW_ROUTING (
    ROUTING_ID NUMBER GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    MAKER_ROLE_ID NUMBER(10,0) NOT NULL, 
    WORKFLOW_CODE VARCHAR2(50) NOT NULL, 
    DESCRIPTION VARCHAR2(255)
);

-- Create the Transitions Table (The engine that dictates the next step)
CREATE TABLE WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS (
    TRANSITION_ID NUMBER GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    WORKFLOW_CODE VARCHAR2(50) NOT NULL,      
    CURRENT_STATE VARCHAR2(50) NOT NULL,      
    ACTION_TAKEN VARCHAR2(50) NOT NULL,       
    NEXT_STATE VARCHAR2(50) NOT NULL,         
    NEXT_ROLE_ID NUMBER(10,0),                
    IS_FINAL_APPROVAL CHAR(1) DEFAULT 'N'     
);

-- Update VOUCHER_POSTING to use numeric Role IDs for the next approver
-- (Assumes your existing column is named NEXT_APPROVAL. If it's different, adjust the name here)
ALTER TABLE VOUCHER_POSTING RENAME COLUMN NEXT_APPROVAL TO OLD_NEXT_APPROVAL;
ALTER TABLE VOUCHER_POSTING ADD NEXT_APPROVAL_ROLE_ID NUMBER(10,0);

COMMIT;

```
### 2. Configure Workflow Routing
Next, we tell the system which workflow applies to which Maker Role. We will use your naming convention (Workflow_3 and Workflow_4).
```sql
-- Role 9001 (TCSGLIF Maker) triggers Workflow_3
INSERT INTO WORKFLOW_ROUTING (MAKER_ROLE_ID, WORKFLOW_CODE, DESCRIPTION) 
VALUES (9001, 'Workflow_3', 'TCS Maker 3-Level Flow');

-- Role 9003 (OTHER Maker) triggers Workflow_4
INSERT INTO WORKFLOW_ROUTING (MAKER_ROLE_ID, WORKFLOW_CODE, DESCRIPTION) 
VALUES (9003, 'Workflow_4', 'Branch Maker 4-Level Flow');

COMMIT;

```
### 3. Configure the Engine Rules (Transitions)
This is the core of the dynamic engine. It completely replaces your Java switch statement. It maps exactly who needs to approve what, and at what step the transaction becomes "POSTED".
#### A. Configure Workflow_3 (3-Level Flow for TCS Makers)
```sql
-- STEP 0: Initialization (When Maker creates the batch) -> Goes to L1 (TCS Check 1: 9001)
INSERT INTO WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS (WORKFLOW_CODE, CURRENT_STATE, ACTION_TAKEN, NEXT_STATE, NEXT_ROLE_ID, IS_FINAL_APPROVAL)
VALUES ('Workflow_3', 'INITIALIZE', 'CREATE', 'PENDING_L1', 9001, 'N');

-- STEP 1: L1 Approves -> Goes to L2 (SBI Check 1: 9002)
INSERT INTO WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS (WORKFLOW_CODE, CURRENT_STATE, ACTION_TAKEN, NEXT_STATE, NEXT_ROLE_ID, IS_FINAL_APPROVAL)
VALUES ('Workflow_3', 'PENDING_L1', 'ACCEPTED', 'PENDING_L2', 9002, 'N');

-- STEP 2: L2 Approves -> Goes to L3 (SBI Check 2: 9002)
INSERT INTO WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS (WORKFLOW_CODE, CURRENT_STATE, ACTION_TAKEN, NEXT_STATE, NEXT_ROLE_ID, IS_FINAL_APPROVAL)
VALUES ('Workflow_3', 'PENDING_L2', 'ACCEPTED', 'PENDING_L3', 9002, 'N');

-- STEP 3: L3 Approves -> POSTED (Final Step, Triggers Oracle Procedure)
INSERT INTO WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS (WORKFLOW_CODE, CURRENT_STATE, ACTION_TAKEN, NEXT_STATE, NEXT_ROLE_ID, IS_FINAL_APPROVAL)
VALUES ('Workflow_3', 'PENDING_L3', 'ACCEPTED', 'POSTED', NULL, 'Y');

-- REJECTIONS for Workflow_3
INSERT INTO WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS (WORKFLOW_CODE, CURRENT_STATE, ACTION_TAKEN, NEXT_STATE, NEXT_ROLE_ID, IS_FINAL_APPROVAL)
VALUES ('Workflow_3', 'PENDING_L1', 'REJECTED', 'REJECTED', NULL, 'N');
INSERT INTO WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS (WORKFLOW_CODE, CURRENT_STATE, ACTION_TAKEN, NEXT_STATE, NEXT_ROLE_ID, IS_FINAL_APPROVAL)
VALUES ('Workflow_3', 'PENDING_L2', 'REJECTED', 'REJECTED', NULL, 'N');
INSERT INTO WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS (WORKFLOW_CODE, CURRENT_STATE, ACTION_TAKEN, NEXT_STATE, NEXT_ROLE_ID, IS_FINAL_APPROVAL)
VALUES ('Workflow_3', 'PENDING_L3', 'REJECTED', 'REJECTED', NULL, 'N');

COMMIT;

```
